@ashutosh-agrawal @StormLiangMS The runtime process-matrix concern was already reviewed with Xichen.

Source-level lifecycle and failure-matrix infrastructure is too large for https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-dhcpmon/pull/111 and remains a separate project. Runtime process-matrix validation belongs to https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-mgmt/pull/26657 after an image containing https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/27277 exists.

The Balanced exact-head Copilot review completed with zero new comments, all visible review threads are resolved, and Azure build 1210811 passed on amd64, arm64, and armhf. We therefore treat this as an acknowledged downstream validation boundary rather than a new blocker for the source PR. Please review the current head.

@Xichen96 Reviewed the downstream reply handling. Confirmed: dhcp4relay broadcasts all downstream replies today (unicast is still a TODO in to_client()), while ISC dhcrelay supports both broadcast and unicast per RFC 1542.

This PR correctly fixes dhcpmon validation without changing relay behavior on the device. On SONiC deployments running dhcp4relay, downstream replies will remain broadcast-only until the relay is updated.

If SONiC itself needs unicast downstream replies, I can follow up in sonic-dhcp-relay/dhcp4relay and open a PR to address that limitation. Please let me know if there’s a functional need.

@Xichen96 Thanks for fixing the multiple-LLA startup failure and adding the 202605 hardware validation.

One concern: skipping `initialize_intf_mac_and_ip_addr()` for the management interface also removes the existing validation that the interface exists. Previously, `SIOCGIFHWADDR` failed initialization for an invalid or stale `-im` value. Now any interface name is accepted; because the sockets bind to all interfaces and packets without a matching device context are ignored, `dhcpmon` could remain healthy while traffic on the real management interface is not monitored.

Could we retain a lightweight existence check, such as `if_nametoindex()`, while continuing to skip MAC/IP address discovery for management interfaces?

@StormLiangMS Implemented the lightweight management-interface existence check as suggested. Management contexts still skip MAC/IP address discovery, but now call `if_nametoindex(ifname)` and fail initialization when the original `-im` value does not identify an existing interface. Using the original argument also ensures overlong names cannot pass via truncation.

202605 manual validation of the functional fix (`942ac44`, CI build `1172862`) confirmed:
- valid `eth0` with two LLAs and no IPv6 GUA: `dhcpmon` remained `RUNNING`;
- missing `-im does-not-exist`: rejected with `No such device`;
- overlong `-im` name: rejected with `No such device`.

The current head only removes two redundant include additions from that implementation; its CI build is running now. Thanks for catching this.

@sumati3031-arista - Reviewed the change; no blockers from my side.

The fix looks correct for dualtor: `giaddr_ip` remains the relay identifier and is set to Loopback0 in dualtor, while outbound DHCP replies toward clients use the VLAN SVI as the L3 source. So keeping `DHCP_CHECK_GIADDR` on `giaddr_ip` and changing `DHCP_CHECK_SRC_IP` to `vlan_ip` matches the packet semantics. In single-ToR, `giaddr_ip == vlan_ip`, so this should preserve existing behavior.

CI is green, and the 202605 backport request is backed by sonic-mgmt issue #25393 with failure details.
